<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sumer</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sumerian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sumer was the region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> where one of the world's earliest civilisations developed, with city-states such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruk">Uruk</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lagash">Lagash</a>. It was conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon of Akkad</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neo-sumerian-empire">Neo-Sumerian Empire</a> describe the revival of Sumerian power under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-dynasty-of-ur">Third Dynasty of Ur</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sumer.jpg" alt="Sumer" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA Overlay: पाटलिपुत्र · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sumer_satellite_map.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
